{"term":"swarm","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:fa0f2ad77d304e96d3","definition":"A large number of insects or other bugs (e.g. centipedes), especially when in motion or (for bees) migrating to a new colony.","example":"[…] reſtleſs thoughts, that like a deadly ſwarm / Of Hornets arm'd […] ruſh upon me thronging,","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"collective","register":"collective","wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0dd19a505b43276896","definition":"A mass of people, animals or things in motion or turmoil.","example":"a swarm of meteorites","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ee6fc0649c91851ab4","definition":"A group of nodes sharing the same torrent in a BitTorrent network.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f210d5fac7c45781d5","definition":"A number of small earthquakes (or other seismic events) occurring, with no clear cause, in a specific area within a relatively short space of time.","example":"Earthquakes were another concern, particularly after swarms were felt in Oklahoma.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e1286420134a42aa6d","definition":"To move as a swarm.","example":"There is an hour or two, after the passengers have embarked, which is disquieting and fussy. Mail bags, so I understand, are being put on board. Stewards, carrying cabin trunks, swarm in the corridors.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["horde"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm","outswarm","overswarm","swarmer","upswarm"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e729fe851e453125bf","definition":"To teem, or be overrun with insects, people, etc.","example":"Every place swarming with soldiers.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm","outswarm","overswarm","swarmer","upswarm"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d3e65e90741e5bc7b0","definition":"To fill a place as a swarm.","example":"All is well until Treorchy, where the platform is swamped by teenagers who have been attending an event. Around four dozen unescorted 12 to 16 year-olds swarm aboard and begin to run riot through the train. Their behaviour is appalling and the presence of CCTV no deterrent.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm","outswarm","overswarm","swarmer","upswarm"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0816d04e102df1bcac","definition":"To overwhelm as by an opposing army.","example":"So, yeah. The overall conclusion of the big gunfight being that, if Yamato is able to tackle the Colorados early, then the Japanese probably have a, maybe a sixty-to-sixty-five-percent chance of pulling this off... although you say \"pulling it off\", it's more a case of \"the Japanese are the last battleship standing\"; they tend to then just get swarmed by angry Fletchers[…]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm","outswarm","overswarm","swarmer","upswarm"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:03e37d378a290e078a","definition":"To climb by gripping with arms and legs alternately.","example":"At the top was placed a piece of money, as a prize for those who could swarm up and seize it.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm","outswarm","overswarm","swarmer","upswarm"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ca2ccdeae3f4f6d09a","definition":"To breed multitudes.","example":"Not ſo thick ſwarm'd once the Soil / Bedropt with blood of Gorgon,","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm","outswarm","overswarm","swarmer","upswarm"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/swɔɹm/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/4e/En-us-swarm.ogg/En-us-swarm.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["afterswarm","aswarm","beeswarm","beswarm","dyke swarm","Dyson swarm","multiswarm","nanoswarm","subswarm","superswarm","swarm intelligence","swarm plot","swarm spore","swarmy","topswarm","outswarm","overswarm","swarmer","upswarm"]}